Section: Tron Light Cycle Game with AI Strategies

Start the game.
Display "Welcome to Tron Light Cycle Game!"
Display "You control the Light Cycle with the arrow keys."
Display "Your goal is to outlast the AI cycles. Avoid crashing!"
Ask the user "How many AI cycles would you like to compete against?"

Set the player's Light Cycle at position (1, 1), color blue.

Let the number of AI cycles be the user's input.
Create a list called "AI Cycles".

For each AI cycle from 1 to the number of AI cycles:
    Create a Light Cycle with a random starting position and random color.
    Assign a random strategy (Trail Chaser, Wall Hugger, or Open Space Seeker).
    Add the AI cycle to the list of AI Cycles.

While the player's Light Cycle is alive and at least one AI cycle is alive:
    For the player's Light Cycle:
        Ask for direction (up, down, left, or right).
        Move the player's Light Cycle in the chosen direction.
        If the player crashes into the wall or a trail, then
            Set the player's Light Cycle to "crashed".
            Display "You crashed! Game Over."

    For each AI cycle in the list:
        If the AI cycle has a "Trail Chaser" strategy, then
            Move the AI cycle towards the player's current position.
            Check if the AI's next move would cause a crash.
            If a crash is likely, adjust direction to avoid it.
        Else if the AI cycle has a "Wall Hugger" strategy, then
            Move the AI cycle along the edge of the arena.
            If near the center, adjust movement towards the wall.
        Else if the AI cycle has an "Open Space Seeker" strategy, then
            Move the AI cycle towards the area with the least number of trails.
            Check the surroundings to find the most open space.
        
        If the AI cycle crashes into a wall or trail, then
            Set the AI cycle to "crashed".
            Remove the AI cycle from the list of active AI cycles.
            Display "An AI cycle has crashed!"

If the player is alive and all AI cycles have crashed, then
    Display "Congratulations, you won!"
Else if the player has crashed, then
    Display "Game Over. You lost."

Ask "Play again? (yes/no)"
If the answer is "yes", then restart the game.
Otherwise, end the game.

Section: Styles
Define a style called "Arena" with grid size 50x50, background color black.
Define a style for the player's Light Cycle with color blue, trail width 3 pixels.
Define a style for AI cycles with random colors, trail width 3 pixels.
